  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on skewness, specifically favoring the lottery where favorable outcomes carry more probability mass—i.e., more left-skewed. In this case, Lottery A is clearly more left-skewed (90% on favorable) compared to B (45% on favorable), so the reason would select A. The individual also emphasizes the high probability of a favorable outcome in A and the lower-than-50% chance in B, aligning their reasoning with the distribution of probabilities over gains. Although the term 'skewness' is not used, the cognitive focus on the concentration of probability on the favorable outcome matches the essence of left-skew preference. The individual does not mention variance, expected value, or regret, but instead emphasizes confidence in winning, which reflects sensitivity to the skew of the distribution. Therefore, the information considered and the justification closely align with the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
